  "Id": 2051,
  "Title": "Victoria standardises the teaching of the birthing process",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Congratulations! Victoria has delivered its 120th baby, by third year student nurses.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Victoria has delivered its 120th baby, by third year student nurses. Congratulations! Through incredible effort and dedication each student gets an individual appointment with a member of the midwifery team to conduct a hands-on session to care for mother and baby before during and after the birthing process. This on-going programme comes at a time when Pakistan has such horrific statistics of perinatal mortality. Our CIME Champion Ms Sadia Karimi needs special mention as the founder member of this programme with other faculty members from SONAM. \"This actually became a source of motivation for us to plan similar experience for the entire class... However, planning simulations for 120 students with limited time and human resource is a challenging task.\""
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In the context of the availability of powerful learning tools such as Victoria, work is currently underway in SONAM to integrate, consolidate, and adequately resource initiatives such as this. Well done to all involved in spearheading this development."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
